404
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:23,160


405
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:23,160


406
00:02:23,010 --> 00:02:27,990
Chaos Theory

407
00:02:23,010 --> 00:02:27,990
Homeostasis

408
00:02:39,230 --> 00:02:42,490
It's hard to believe that May Queen used to be here.

409
00:02:42,490 --> 00:02:44,650
May Queen? That a potato?

410
00:02:44,650 --> 00:02:47,160
During summer, I prefer noodles to potatoes.

411
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:50,160
It isn't a potato...

412
00:02:50,820 --> 00:02:55,540
If May Queen never existed, then how did we meet Feyris?

413
00:02:55,540 --> 00:03:00,880
Well, it's thanks to potato ramen that we met her.

414
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:02,510
What do you mean?

415
00:03:02,510 --> 00:03:04,090
You've forgotten?

416
00:03:04,090 --> 00:03:06,800
The day of the Rai-Net Tournament in Ikebukuro,

417
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:10,180
I got sick from the potato ramen I had for lunch,

418
00:03:10,180 --> 00:03:11,560
so I withdrew.

419
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:12,220
And then?

420
00:03:12,220 --> 00:03:15,560
Mayushii and you entered as a pair,

421
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:18,190
and you went up against Feyris-tan.

422
00:03:18,710 --> 00:03:20,860
You totally lost,

423
00:03:20,860 --> 00:03:24,780
but Mayushii and Feyris-tan became friends.

424
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:26,450
I see.

425
00:03:26,450 --> 00:03:28,240
Look, look, Ruka-chan.

426
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:30,990
I bought this cosplayer photo book yesterday, in Nakano!

427
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:34,040
So cute...

428
00:03:32,370 --> 00:03:38,700
<i>The past changed, but our relationships haven't?</i>

429
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:41,000
You seem to have lots of time

430
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,130
on your hands, this Obon, Lab Member Girls.

431
00:03:44,130 --> 00:03:45,630
Hello, there.

432
00:03:45,630 --> 00:03:47,180
Look! Cute, huh?

433
00:03:47,180 --> 00:03:50,430
Hey! It's Sedona from <i>Blood Tune</i>!

434
00:03:50,930 --> 00:03:52,470
It's really detailed!

435
00:03:52,470 --> 00:03:53,890
There's a swimsuit version, too.

436
00:03:53,890 --> 00:03:55,560
I wish I could be like that.

437
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:57,810
I don't have those proportions.

438
00:03:57,810 --> 00:03:58,770
It's okay!

439
00:03:58,770 --> 00:04:00,400
Flat is justice!

440
00:04:02,110 --> 00:04:03,070
I know!

441
00:04:03,070 --> 00:04:04,610
Why not take all the lab members,

442
00:04:04,610 --> 00:04:06,110
and go to the beach?

443
00:04:06,110 --> 00:04:07,310
With Kurisu-chan!

444
00:04:07,810 --> 00:04:09,630
Everyone wears their school swimsuits, okay?

445
00:04:09,630 --> 00:04:12,470
I'm not going swimming with a pervert.

446
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:17,790
Um, well... I mean, if it's just the girls,

447
00:04:17,790 --> 00:04:20,120
I'd love to!

448
00:04:20,960 --> 00:04:23,290
Why not be honest, Christina?

449
00:04:23,290 --> 00:04:24,340
You don't want

450
00:04:24,340 --> 00:04:26,760
anyone to see the mole on your rear,

451
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:29,340
so you can't go.

452
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:31,430
There's no mole!

453
00:04:31,430 --> 00:04:34,720
And if it's just the girls,

454
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:36,840
then Rukako can't go.

455
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:37,930
Huh? Why not?

456
00:04:37,930 --> 00:04:40,230
I told you earlier, right?

457
00:04:40,230 --> 00:04:42,440
That Rukako's actually a guy.

458
00:04:53,410 --> 00:04:55,620
You know, you're a jerk.

459
00:04:55,990 --> 00:04:58,330
How can you call a girl a guy?

460
00:04:58,330 --> 00:05:01,750
Mayushii doesn't like it when you say stuff like that.

461
00:05:01,750 --> 00:05:03,330
Isn't that really mean?

462
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:07,690
Wait!

463
00:05:07,690 --> 00:05:08,690
Why are you crying?

464
00:05:08,690 --> 00:05:11,530
Apologize to Urushibara-san. Now.

465
00:05:11,530 --> 00:05:12,470
No, seriously.

466
00:05:12,470 --> 00:05:14,230
Why would I apologize? It's trueâ

467
00:05:14,230 --> 00:05:15,310
It's fine!

468
00:05:15,970 --> 00:05:19,770
So that's what you think of me, Okabe-san.

469
00:05:19,770 --> 00:05:22,740
No, no, no, Rukako! You're really...

470
00:05:21,940 --> 00:05:23,150
How long will you keep that up?

471
00:05:23,150 --> 00:05:24,900
I'm going home!

472
00:05:24,900 --> 00:05:26,210
Wait!

473
00:05:26,210 --> 00:05:27,900
You're a guy!

474
00:05:27,900 --> 00:05:31,340
Look! Right here, you have...

475
00:05:34,490 --> 00:05:36,490
It's gone! There's nothing here!

476
00:05:36,490 --> 00:05:39,230
Okabe-san, stop it...

477
00:05:41,580 --> 00:05:45,380
Rukako, you're a girl?

478
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:50,210
I've been saying that this whole time!

479
00:05:53,090 --> 00:05:56,180
Hey... What's wrong?

480
00:05:56,180 --> 00:05:57,600
Don't worry about it.

481
00:05:57,600 --> 00:05:59,560
Just a bit of torture...

482
00:05:58,310 --> 00:05:59,560
Torture?

483
00:05:59,560 --> 00:06:01,480
By Makise Kurisu?

484
00:06:02,140 --> 00:06:05,020
Yes, but I fixed the misunderstanding.

485
00:06:05,020 --> 00:06:06,060
I think...

486
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:07,730
She got your legs?

487
00:06:08,900 --> 00:06:10,990
Don't touch my legs!

488
00:06:10,990 --> 00:06:13,780
She made me sit on my knees for an hour!

489
00:06:13,780 --> 00:06:17,660
No! I mean, I was tortured.

490
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:22,250
Oh... That isn't torture.

491
00:06:22,250 --> 00:06:26,500
You almost sound like you've been tortured.

492
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:28,170
Well, I am a soldier.

493
00:06:35,550 --> 00:06:37,880
It's a perfect day for cycling...

494
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:39,930
Yeah?

495
00:06:42,810 --> 00:06:43,940
Hey...

496
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:46,100
Want to go for a ride?

497
00:06:53,700 --> 00:06:57,770
Is this what you call cycling?

498
00:06:59,780 --> 00:07:05,580
I came to Tokyo to find my dad.

499
00:07:05,580 --> 00:07:07,040
To find him?

500
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:09,040
Did he disappear or something?

501
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:11,130
I haven't seen him in years.

502
00:07:11,130 --> 00:07:12,910
I can't even remember his face.

503
00:07:13,430 --> 00:07:16,180
But I know he's in this city.

504
00:07:16,180 --> 00:07:18,140
This is my only clue...

505
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:21,550
A badge he used to own.

506
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:25,520
Then you shouldn't just kill time at a part-time job, should you?

507
00:07:26,730 --> 00:07:28,900
There's some stuff going on, you know?

508
00:07:28,900 --> 00:07:31,650
But there's one chance.

509
00:07:33,610 --> 00:07:37,610
My dad might show up tomorrow, at a certain place.

510
00:07:38,160 --> 00:07:42,790
If I miss that, I'll have to leave this town.

511
00:07:43,540 --> 00:07:46,080
There's somewhere I have to go.

512
00:07:46,080 --> 00:07:48,410
I'm busy, you know?

513
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:53,760
Well, I was always planning on giving up if I couldn't meet him.

514
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:57,680
You're uneasy, aren't you?

515
00:07:57,680 --> 00:07:59,890
I can understand that feeling.

516
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:01,470
But too bad, part-time soldier!

517
00:08:02,350 --> 00:08:04,350
Your luck ran out, the minute

518
00:08:04,350 --> 00:08:08,600
you spoke to the great Mad Scientist, Hououin Kyouma.

519
00:08:09,650 --> 00:08:12,820
You are now Lab Member 008!

520
00:08:13,420 --> 00:08:15,400
You will be our guinea pig.

521
00:08:15,860 --> 00:08:17,530
Wh-What are you going to do?

522
00:08:17,530 --> 00:08:19,570
Change the past.

523
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:21,700
You may think me cruel if you like.

524
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:24,790
But there is no escape for you.

525
00:08:24,790 --> 00:08:29,420
Send a D-mail to your father, before he leaves.

526
00:08:29,420 --> 00:08:32,420
Tell him not to leave his daughter behind.

527
00:08:35,460 --> 00:08:37,470
You're a good person, you know that?

528
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:38,670
What?

529
00:08:39,180 --> 00:08:43,100
I feel a bit better now, somehow.

530
00:08:45,060 --> 00:08:47,020
I have to get back.

531
00:08:47,020 --> 00:08:49,560
Thanks for talking to me!

532
00:08:50,060 --> 00:08:51,100
Listen!

533
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:53,310
Whether you see him tomorrow or not,

534
00:08:53,310 --> 00:08:54,730
come by the lab!

535
00:08:54,730 --> 00:08:56,440
I will use your sentimentality

536
00:08:56,440 --> 00:08:58,400
for an experiment with the D-mail!

537
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:02,480
You really are a mad scientist!

538
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:04,310
That's terrible...

539
00:09:13,630 --> 00:09:16,500
I will now explain

540
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:19,550
the parameters of Operation EldhrÃ­mnir.

541
00:09:19,550 --> 00:09:21,260
More Norse myths?

542
00:09:21,760 --> 00:09:23,930
If the part-time warrior meets her father,

543
00:09:23,930 --> 00:09:25,300
we'll hold a celebration...

544
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:27,930
A last supper in Tokyo, for her.

545
00:09:28,310 --> 00:09:29,230
And if she doesn't,

546
00:09:29,230 --> 00:09:31,520
we will try to cheer her up,

547
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:33,770
and then send a D-mail.

548
00:09:34,520 --> 00:09:35,730
Where's Daru?

549
00:09:36,150 --> 00:09:37,900
He's meeting his online friends tonight,

550
00:09:37,900 --> 00:09:39,320
so he said he can't join us.

551
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:40,990
The fool!

552
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:44,070
But I've taken steps.

553
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:48,590
Daru

554
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:48,590
Now is the time to choose

555
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:48,590
Now is the time to choose

556
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:48,590
Feyris's cooking or your meeting.
Which will you choose?

557
00:09:44,660 --> 00:09:47,030
I sent this message.

558
00:09:47,030 --> 00:09:49,620
Feyris's cooking or your meeting.

559
00:09:49,620 --> 00:09:51,250
Which will you choose?

560
00:09:51,250 --> 00:09:54,580
But Feyris-chan can't come, right?

561
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,300
Feyris has never met the part-time warrior,

562
00:09:57,300 --> 00:09:58,920
so it can't be helped.

563
00:09:58,920 --> 00:10:01,470
But Daru has a duty to participate in this operation.

564
00:10:01,470 --> 00:10:06,850
Um... I've never met this Suzuha-san...

565
00:10:06,850 --> 00:10:07,640
That's fine.

566
00:10:08,180 --> 00:10:11,230
I'm sending you all shopping for the banquet.

567
00:10:11,230 --> 00:10:12,060
And you?

568
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:14,230
I will follow the part-time warrior

569
00:10:14,230 --> 00:10:16,310
and report in on the situation.

570
00:10:16,310 --> 00:10:17,730
Don't you dare.

571
00:10:17,730 --> 00:10:20,070
Let the father and daughter have their time together.

572
00:10:20,070 --> 00:10:21,530
That's right.

573
00:10:21,530 --> 00:10:23,450
Come shopping with us!

574
00:10:23,450 --> 00:10:24,660
I'm following herâ

575
00:10:24,660 --> 00:10:26,410
I said no!

576
00:10:26,410 --> 00:10:29,520
Don't tell me what to do, assistant...

577
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:31,620
You want to sit on your knees again?

578
00:10:32,410 --> 00:10:34,120
This time, for three hours...

579
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:36,580
Now, then! Let's get things ready for the party!

580
00:10:43,030 --> 00:10:44,270
I'm watching you.

581
00:10:44,300 --> 00:10:44,770
I'm watching

582
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:45,270
watching you.

583
00:10:50,140 --> 00:10:51,930
What's wrong, Okarin?

584
00:10:52,430 --> 00:10:53,430
Nothing.

585
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:54,830
I'm watching you.

586
00:11:00,980 --> 00:11:02,150
<i>What is this?</i>

587
00:11:11,540 --> 00:11:14,130
<i>I think sweet curry is good.</i>

588
00:11:14,130 --> 00:11:15,830
<i>Or maybe spicy?</i>

589
00:11:15,830 --> 00:11:17,460
<i>What do you think?</i>

590
00:11:17,460 --> 00:11:21,090
<i>S-Sure... Spicy, I guess.</i>

591
00:11:21,090 --> 00:11:24,840
<i>Oh, yeah! Suzu-san's a part-time warrior, right?</i>

592
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:27,720
<i>If she's a warrior, she'll want spicy.</i>

593
00:11:28,140 --> 00:11:31,470
<i>Um... Next, we need the meat.</i>

594
00:11:33,660 --> 00:11:36,140
<i>Beef is expensive...</i>

595
00:11:38,060 --> 00:11:39,480
Hey, Okarin.

596
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:41,460
You don't look good.

597
00:11:41,990 --> 00:11:43,690
Back there, you would've normally said...

598
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:47,990
"The Organization's sabotage has increased the price of beef!

599
00:11:47,990 --> 00:11:52,370
Has Operation Time Sale begun?"

600
00:11:55,750 --> 00:11:59,290
But you use Norse mythology there, not "time sale."

601
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:01,000
It's me.

602
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:04,260
The Organization's sabotage has caused unexpected expenses

603
00:12:04,260 --> 00:12:06,300
in Operation Audhumbla.

604
00:12:06,300 --> 00:12:09,010
I'm requesting additional funds for the operation.

605
00:12:10,590 --> 00:12:12,050
The first star!

606
00:12:13,890 --> 00:12:15,730
Venus?

607
00:12:18,480 --> 00:12:19,900
Hey, Okarin?

608
00:12:21,060 --> 00:12:23,270
Remember in elementary school,

609
00:12:23,270 --> 00:12:25,740
when you got really sick, with a high fever?

610
00:12:26,530 --> 00:12:31,200
Yes. The world was panicking over the Y2K problem.

611
00:12:31,820 --> 00:12:38,410
Mayushii was really scared you would die then.

612
00:12:39,500 --> 00:12:42,250
So I prayed to the sky.

613
00:12:43,250 --> 00:12:47,170
And then, there was a falling star.

614
00:12:48,510 --> 00:12:50,550
I said to the falling star,

615
00:12:50,550 --> 00:12:53,930
"Don't die, Okarin!" three times.

616
00:12:54,560 --> 00:12:58,770
And the next day, you got better!

617
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:03,310
And so I saved your life.

618
00:13:04,270 --> 00:13:05,730
No, that's not true.

619
00:13:05,730 --> 00:13:07,570
It was the choice of Steins Gate

620
00:13:07,570 --> 00:13:09,570
that I survived back then.

621
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:12,700
Was it?

622
00:13:12,700 --> 00:13:13,990
It was.

623
00:13:13,990 --> 00:13:15,450
I see.

624
00:13:16,330 --> 00:13:19,160
Hey, remember what you said,

625
00:13:19,160 --> 00:13:21,500
when you got sick and collapsed?

626
00:13:22,170 --> 00:13:25,750
"Everything I saw began to flow together,

627
00:13:25,750 --> 00:13:30,630
and suddenly, I shook and couldn't stand up."

628
00:13:31,130 --> 00:13:33,640
You looked just like that

629
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:35,840
in Feyris-chan's condominium.

630
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:39,480
<i>That feeling I had when I got that fever</i>

631
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:44,020
<i>was just like the feeling I get when I move world lines.</i>

632
00:13:44,690 --> 00:13:45,860
<i>Which means...</i>

633
00:13:45,860 --> 00:13:49,070
<i>I attained my magic eye, Reading Steiner,</i>

634
00:13:49,070 --> 00:13:51,990
<i>at that moment?</i>

635
00:13:56,160 --> 00:13:57,370
We're back!

636
00:13:57,370 --> 00:13:58,740
Welcome back.

637
00:13:59,750 --> 00:14:01,460
You smell something weird?

638
00:14:01,460 --> 00:14:05,080
I think it's the smell of Kurisu-san's apple pie.

639
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:05,790
What?

640
00:14:05,790 --> 00:14:06,790
This?

641
00:14:06,790 --> 00:14:08,420
Want Mayushii to help, too?

642
00:14:08,420 --> 00:14:10,630
Can you boil an egg?

643
00:14:10,630 --> 00:14:12,010
Sure!

644
00:14:12,010 --> 00:14:16,510
Um... Can I use the microwave?

645
00:14:16,510 --> 00:14:17,930
N-No!

646
00:14:17,930 --> 00:14:20,050
If you put drop a raw egg in, it will explode!

647
00:14:20,050 --> 00:14:21,640
I'll make the egg.

648
00:14:22,690 --> 00:14:24,850
So you chop up the mushrooms, Mayuri.

649
00:14:24,850 --> 00:14:25,940
Okay!

650
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:27,270
W-Wait!

651
00:14:27,270 --> 00:14:29,860
You don't need mushrooms or boiled eggs for apple pie!

652
00:14:29,860 --> 00:14:31,900
It's for the salad, to go with it.

653
00:14:31,900 --> 00:14:36,570
I don't think a boiled egg and mushroom salad really goes with apple pie.

654
00:14:37,070 --> 00:14:37,950
And you!

655
00:14:37,950 --> 00:14:39,660
Stop chopping up mushrooms over there!

656
00:14:39,660 --> 00:14:40,660
Move!

657
00:14:43,290 --> 00:14:44,370
It's me.

658
00:14:44,370 --> 00:14:47,880
It seems I've released the seals that bound a dark god.

659
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:51,130
If I don't contact you within the hour,

660
00:14:51,130 --> 00:14:54,880
tell my parents that I loved them.

661
00:14:54,880 --> 00:14:57,550
Okabe-san, do you have a rice cooker?

662
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:00,470
Where's Feyris-tan?

663
00:15:00,810 --> 00:15:02,430
Where's Feyris-tan?

664
00:15:02,430 --> 00:15:05,100
Hashida, you've been deceived.

665
00:15:05,100 --> 00:15:07,270
Feyris-san said she couldn't come.

666
00:15:07,270 --> 00:15:08,860
Seriously?

667
00:15:08,860 --> 00:15:09,700
Hey, Okarin!

668
00:15:10,070 --> 00:15:12,530
Next time I get a chance, I'll take care of it.

669
00:15:12,530 --> 00:15:14,110
Screw you!

670
00:15:14,110 --> 00:15:16,490
I was really looking forward to my time machine forum meeting.

671
00:15:16,490 --> 00:15:18,370
Time machine forum?

672
00:15:18,370 --> 00:15:22,620
It's with a sci-fi message board I frequent a lot.

673
00:15:22,620 --> 00:15:25,120
A professional author was supposed to go, too!

674
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:27,790
This is an interestingly shaped mess kit.

675
00:15:28,210 --> 00:15:29,130
Don't touch it.

676
00:15:29,130 --> 00:15:30,500
That's not a mess kit.

677
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:32,760
It's Future Gadget #4, The Moad Snake.

678
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:33,710
A claymore mine?

679
00:15:33,710 --> 00:15:35,510
It's made to look like one.

680
00:15:35,510 --> 00:15:36,970
It's a super-instant humidifier.

681
00:15:36,970 --> 00:15:38,260
Oh, this?

682
00:15:38,260 --> 00:15:39,420
S-Stop! Don't!

683
00:15:50,520 --> 00:15:52,730
I'm sorry, Okabe-san.

684
00:15:52,730 --> 00:15:54,570
Don't worry about it.

685
00:15:54,570 --> 00:15:56,860
Next time, don't touch it.

686
00:15:56,860 --> 00:15:59,780
Hey, couldn't we use this?

687
00:16:00,490 --> 00:16:02,740
A vacuum cleaner?

688
00:16:02,740 --> 00:16:04,080
Nope!

689
00:16:04,080 --> 00:16:05,790
It's Future Gadget #3.

690
00:16:05,790 --> 00:16:07,080
Or #2?

691
00:16:07,080 --> 00:16:08,330
#5!

692
00:16:08,330 --> 00:16:09,580
And its name is

693
00:16:09,580 --> 00:16:11,630
"Once Again I've Connected Something Useless

694
00:16:11,630 --> 00:16:12,840
By Goemon."

695
00:16:13,340 --> 00:16:17,680
We made it so you can use a vacuum cleaner's output to warm a dryer.

696
00:16:17,680 --> 00:16:18,780
Give it to me.

697
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:20,510
Wait!

698
00:16:20,510 --> 00:16:22,180
When you use that, you need to turn off

699
00:16:22,180 --> 00:16:23,210
any other appliances, or...

700
00:16:24,770 --> 00:16:26,350
...it'll trigger the breaker.

701
00:16:27,690 --> 00:16:30,350
Where's the flashlight?

702
00:16:30,810 --> 00:16:31,650
Is this it?

703
00:16:31,650 --> 00:16:32,940
No, Miss Ruka.

704
00:16:32,940 --> 00:16:34,230
That's a daikon radish.

705
00:16:34,940 --> 00:16:37,150
U-Um, where's the breaker?

706
00:16:37,150 --> 00:16:38,780
If you walk around...

707
00:16:41,280 --> 00:16:42,620
I told you...

708
00:16:43,030 --> 00:16:44,490
Ow...

709
00:16:44,490 --> 00:16:45,870
The breaker's in the front hall.

710
00:16:48,830 --> 00:16:50,040
Are you okay?

711
00:16:55,420 --> 00:16:56,760
What's so funny?

712
00:16:57,460 --> 00:16:58,840
I'm sorry.

713
00:16:58,840 --> 00:17:00,380
But...

714
00:17:01,590 --> 00:17:04,220
The lab I worked at in America had some of

715
00:17:04,220 --> 00:17:07,770
the best people from around the world.

716
00:17:07,770 --> 00:17:09,850
But they all had really big heads,

717
00:17:09,850 --> 00:17:12,150
so it was a really hostile place.

718
00:17:12,980 --> 00:17:17,230
Compared to them, your lab is really childish,

719
00:17:17,230 --> 00:17:18,570
but it's a fun place to be.

720
00:17:19,860 --> 00:17:22,990
I-I'm not praising you, okay?

721
00:17:22,990 --> 00:17:27,160
I was just kinda thinking that...

722
00:17:27,700 --> 00:17:31,210
I guess maybe I simply wanted friends.

723
00:17:35,090 --> 00:17:37,000
I, um...

724
00:17:37,780 --> 00:17:39,700
I think of you as a companion.

725
00:17:41,050 --> 00:17:43,340
You told me before, didn't you?

726
00:17:43,720 --> 00:17:46,350
That I was your dear companion.

727
00:17:46,930 --> 00:17:50,140
That made me really happy, I guess.

728
00:17:54,230 --> 00:17:55,900
You got a fever?

729
00:17:56,630 --> 00:17:57,940
N-No!

730
00:17:57,940 --> 00:18:00,860
What? I'm trying to rethink my opinion of you...

731
00:18:00,860 --> 00:18:02,310
Stupid Okabe!

732
00:18:14,630 --> 00:18:16,790
Suzu-san's late.

733
00:18:16,790 --> 00:18:19,090
I wonder if she met her dad.

734
00:18:19,090 --> 00:18:22,250
I bet they're finally spending time together.

735
00:18:22,550 --> 00:18:26,390
I told her to come to the lab, either way.

736
00:18:27,260 --> 00:18:28,970
But it's late.

737
00:18:29,770 --> 00:18:31,310
We're aborting the operation.

738
00:18:31,310 --> 00:18:32,610
You guys, go on home.

739
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:47,970
Part-Time Warrior

740
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:47,970
Part-Time Warrior

